1
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:15,057
I'm on a journey out to see
the world While I'm on my own,

2
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:19,780
I've yet to reach the end So won't
you come along with me right now?

3
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:23,717
Surely then we can!

4
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,780
Follow me now as we
journey on from sea to sea

5
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:32,220
For that treasure known
by everybody as one piece.

6
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:37,440
Even though they laugh and
say it's just a fantasy.

7
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,857
We are going, there's no doubt we go.

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:45,200
Cause we can feel the
rush of energy overcome.

9
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:48,300
It will lead the way.

10
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:53,480
Keep pretending that you know what to do.

11
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:57,397
Books will only get in the way.

12
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:00,020
No guides for today.

13
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:02,437
Do not worry soon.

14
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,977
The rain will be gone with the wind.

15
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:05,717
Keep your chin up, raise the anchor.

16
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:06,630
Now that's what you'll do.

17
00:01:06,713 --> 00:01:07,777
Give it time and calm.

18
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,297
The storm that you have built within.

19
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:11,417
Come and have not forget number two.

20
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:13,557
Once tomorrow's wind picks up.

21
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:14,757
We set self cause we can't.

22
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:15,897
Fresh enough, stand tall.

23
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:17,277
And take a look at one of you.

24
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,657
All the journey makes
me want to see somebody.

25
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,681
There are things out there
you just won't believe.

26
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,760
Beyond your wildest dreams.

27
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,297
Don't think for a second.

28
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:30,780
It's not the truth.

29
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:32,797
That's the story.

30
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:34,657
Most will believe.

31
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:36,077
Not me.

32
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:37,420
Come and see.

33
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:40,777
I am on a journey.

34
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:42,317
Out to see the world.

35
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,317
Don't all on my own.

36
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,337
I've got my group of friends.

37
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:47,357
Together we've got our way.

38
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,957
That's how it's done.

39
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,017
Says your captain.

40
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,277
Who says it can't be done.

41
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,937
We haven't even tried.

42
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:53,937
Gotta just believe.

43
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:55,937
We'll make it to the end.

44
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,577
I just wanna do it all right now.

45
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:00,817
Together surely we can.

46
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,717
Yes, we can.

47
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,097
You can.

48
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:06,717
Just take this moment in.

49
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,057
We can.

50
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:09,437
I can.

51
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:12,217
Just take this feeling in.

52
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:13,477
Right now.

53
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:14,900
Right now.

54
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:18,700
Oh yes, we can.

55
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:26,330
Yes, we can!

56
00:02:26,413 --> 00:02:27,243
Yes, we can!

57
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:33,797
Those two are gonna find the mink tribe.

58
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,977
And when they do, they're
gonna ask about Raizo.

59
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:37,766
Then we're all super screwed!

60
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:39,250
Indeed.

61
00:02:39,333 --> 00:02:42,317
The search for some samurai who
wasn't even here was devastating.

62
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,857
The Mokumo duktum was
destroyed as collateral damage.

63
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:45,770
Let's hurry.

64
00:02:45,853 --> 00:02:47,057
It might not be too late.

65
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:48,880
Right, off we go then.

66
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:04,640
This is nothing to monkey around about!

67
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,920
That's the visitor's bell!

68
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,860
Samurai! Samurai! Samurai!

69
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,240
We'll head to the city.

70
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:25,597
Tell anyone who is capable to follow me.

71
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:26,510
Sir!

72
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:31,377
Duke Dogstorm, a warning is ready
to go with your command, sir.

73
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:32,290
Good.

74
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:50,760
That bell is rather cacophonous, isn't it?

75
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,500
Not to mention ceaseless.

76
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:56,158
I believe it is to announce
the arrival of a visitor.

77
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:59,020
They must be welcoming us to their land.

78
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:00,840
How reassuring.

79
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:08,840
But I confess, Sir Law's
words leave me uncertain.

80
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:13,640
The allegedly human-hating inhabitants
here are actually the minks?

81
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,070
Yes.

82
00:04:15,153 --> 00:04:17,337
It's not that I doubt the
words of our associate,

83
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:20,302
but it just doesn't seem
to make any sense to me.

84
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:23,873
If that's what people say,
then I wonder what happened...

85
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,060
Hello, Father!

86
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:32,540
Good to see you!

87
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:35,090
Momonosuke!

88
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:37,780
Kanjuro, too!

89
00:04:38,060 --> 00:04:40,060
We are reunited at long last!

90
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:41,670
Indeed.

91
00:04:41,753 --> 00:04:42,848
So sorry to make you worry.

92
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,777
Are you not with Sir Luffy?

93
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:46,448
Why are you here all alone?

94
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,500
To be quite honest,

95
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:52,617
I have been ill at ease ever since
we first set foot upon this land.

96
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:55,857
So I have been sleeping in a
room apart from the others.

97
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:56,770
Poor thing.

98
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:58,420
I'm pained to hear it.

99
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:01,180
When I awoke moments ago, I was alone.

100
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:03,754
So I went searching to find the others.

101
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,917
Curious that the others are missing,

102
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,937
but it's likely they're simply
preparing a welcome for us.

103
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:10,680
That is doubtless the case.

104
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:16,257
Why do I have to run before breakfast?

105
00:05:16,340 --> 00:05:17,170
I told you!

106
00:05:17,253 --> 00:05:19,180
Cause Kin'emon and what's his name?

107
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:20,520
It's Kanjuro!

108
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:21,990
Right!

109
00:05:22,073 --> 00:05:23,386
Kin'emon and Kanjuro are here!

110
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:25,497
The whole country's already in an uproar,

111
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:27,977
ringing the visitor's bell
and yelling about samurai!

112
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:29,217
To make matters worse,

113
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:32,597
Cat Viper is running to the city
with a team of guardians as we speak!

114
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:34,217
Think we'll get another feast?

115
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:36,577
Sure would be awesome
to do two days in a row!

116
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:37,737
I'm willing to fight!

117
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:38,650
Obviously!

118
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:41,497
And I can't blame them.

119
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:45,980
They were wrongly accused of hiding
a samurai and nearly died for it.

120
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,057
Where are the samurai?

121
00:05:59,140 --> 00:06:01,377
We'll find them right away, sir.

122
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:06,401
People are coming here from all directions,
so they should catch them along the way.

123
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:13,990
Pedro!

124
00:06:14,073 --> 00:06:14,903
What do you see?

125
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:19,160
This is bad.

126
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:27,525
Still haven't heard any
word about the samurai?

127
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:29,328
My men are on the hunt now.

128
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,306
Master, we have to pull back!

129
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:32,800
Why would I do that?

130
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,020
Hurry, please!

131
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,517
I don't see anything here.

132
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:39,120
Please, just keep walking.

133
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:06,200
They've noticed each other!

134
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,361
There's no escaping fate anymore!

135
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:16,820
Master, your grace.

136
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:20,437
It's not worth it, don't fight.

137
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:23,300
Please calm down, you're
both still injured.

138
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:30,700
Some manner of altercation.

139
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,580
It can't be?

140
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:48,220
oh man that was close crazy close!

141
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:54,020
you're in danger, don't say another
word and go back to the sunny quickly.

142
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:58,717
how many years has it been?

143
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,417
you gotta look like a wreck,

144
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:05,877
you're one to talk, mutt seems you're.

145
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:08,313
I'm missing one of your legs down there.

146
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:12,192
Somebody stop him quick!

147
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,988
Well, it's not gonna be me!

148
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:17,660
Where is Raizo?

149
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:19,440
Hand him over already.

150
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:21,819
I know you're hiding him somewhere.

151
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:25,800
Let me say it one more time.

152
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,500
There is no Raizo here!

153
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:30,337
Search through the country as
much as you, Karoo, please!

154
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:32,060
But you'll find no samurai!

155
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:41,600
I wonder if you'll say goodbye to this leg
first, or tell us where the samurai is.

156
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:44,777
I'm gonna keep hacking away
until you give me what I want.

157
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:46,742
So what's it gonna be, Dog King?

158
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:50,160
Give up Raizo, or give up your leg?

159
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:00,560
There's nothing I can do.

160
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:03,880
So take the damned leg if you got or must.

161
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:09,520
What can you gotta do with one hand?

162
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,740
You certainly can't defeat me.

163
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:15,320
Go back to your lasagna
and eat yourself to death.

164
00:09:16,540 --> 00:09:17,680
Out with it!

165
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:19,280
Where is Race?

166
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:21,300
How the hell should I know?

167
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:25,227
Someone from the land of Wano
has no business in this country.

168
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:27,260
They can't even fight.

169
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:30,522
You gotta make sure of
that with your poison gas.

170
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:32,600
But you cowardly curse!

171
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:38,032
Crap, you don't think he's
gonna break the chains, do you?

172
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,760
Is the gas really working?

173
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:41,416
Immobilize his arms!

174
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:43,920
Better hurry, I'm breaking free!

175
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:49,500
My people are no threat to you,
Karoo, but I won't go down so easy!

176
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,617
No, Master, you'll die!

177
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:53,920
Wanna stab someone?

178
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:57,620
I'll take every last spear you've got!

179
00:09:59,020 --> 00:09:59,850
Master!

180
00:10:06,660 --> 00:10:10,897
I was so sad when I found out that
you gotta had lost one of your legs.

181
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:14,420
Cause I was hoping you gotta
would lose your life instead.

182
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:17,477
This land ain't got room for two kings.

183
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:19,980
You've said enough, please stop it.

184
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:24,320
Well we can get rid of one
now, since we're both here.

185
00:10:26,260 --> 00:10:28,920
I've been waiting for this day. Huh?

186
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,500
A dog and a cat? Hey!

187
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:44,220
I heard those two were
strong, but this is scary.

188
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:50,640
Stop fighting now!

189
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:55,320
Oh, Greg, you ruined everything you don't!

190
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:56,420
It's true.

191
00:10:58,900 --> 00:10:59,980
A summoner!

192
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,540
I hope you're happy now!

193
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,528
They're all gonna kill you!

194
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:10,180
Come on, run away!

195
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,070
Momo!

196
00:11:13,153 --> 00:11:14,786
Release me from your missile!

197
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,780
Why do all of you have a death wish?

198
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:19,220
Momonosuke, wait!

199
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:20,610
Kanjino!

200
00:11:20,693 --> 00:11:21,557
What are you doing?

201
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:24,140
You gotta get out of here! Run! Hurry!

202
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:28,920
Cat Viper!

203
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:30,737
Dubstorm, just listen to me!

204
00:11:30,820 --> 00:11:33,702
They don't mean this
country any harm, I promise!

205
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:42,560
I am the Samurai Kin'emon, a
loyal retainer of the Kozuki clan.

206
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:44,945
hailing from the land of Wano.

207
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:50,600
I am here to reunite with my
comrade Raizo, a fellow warrior.

208
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,517
Can he be found in this land?

209
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:53,430
Look, he's not here!

210
00:11:53,513 --> 00:11:56,297
The country was practically
destroyed because of it, you moron!

211
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:57,210
Do something.

212
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:58,470
On it.

213
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:15,620
Oh, I've longed for this day.

214
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:21,820
I swear on my honor,
I don't owe this Race.

215
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:31,220
If the man you're talking about is
here, then you can take my life!

216
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:36,840
So Raizo is here.

217
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:39,180
And he is well.

218
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,960
I'm glad to hear it.

219
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:58,239
Thank you, friend.

220
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,357
Hey, hold on, you two!

221
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:10,558
You're telling me Rhizo has
been here from the start,

222
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:13,600
and you all knew the whole country?!

223
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:26,740
But, but, you all nearly died and
nobody here said a single word!

224
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:30,940
This city stood for a thousand
years and now it's ruined!

225
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:41,980
I'm sorry, but we had to keep
it secret even from you, Karoo.

226
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:47,724
For many years, we have been like family
to the Kozuki clan from the land of Wano.

227
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:53,455
There's nothing that can't be rebuilt.

228
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:55,992
Our people would never sell out a friend.

229
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:11,457
Reports claim he attacked the Navy vessel

230
00:14:11,540 --> 00:14:15,540
transporting Doe Flamingo
and was soundly defeated.

231
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,140
That's bullshit!

232
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:19,110
Hey! Sir!

233
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:22,700
Tell me, do I look dead to you?

234
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:25,500
Uh, no, not at all!

235
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:27,420
You look very alive!

236
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:49,340
Allow me to offer proof of our bond.

237
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:58,460
No mistake,

238
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:00,397
the crest of the Kozuki clan,

239
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:03,715
for I have seen it upon our
two kings and Race as well.

240
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:09,210
Kozuki.

241
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:11,889
Well, jeez, that didn't
go like we thought.

242
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:18,237
I was getting ready for a fight, but
it turns out they're best buddies.

243
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:19,150
Who knew?

244
00:15:19,233 --> 00:15:20,336
It's no one's fault.

245
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:23,800
We may be allies, but some
secrets have to be kept.

246
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:25,310
Wow.

247
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:29,297
So the doggy and the kitty have
the same hidden crest as Kin'emon?

248
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:33,262
If the bond they share is that
strong, it must be quite the story.

249
00:15:34,220 --> 00:15:35,050
Dogstorm.

250
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:37,060
Cat Viper. I'm surprised.

251
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:43,880
I wasn't certain I would find you
two alive and well, but here you are.

252
00:15:44,060 --> 00:15:48,648
We kept the faith, although death would
have been a mercy after what happened.

253
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:53,700
Well, if we waited here, we knew
we'd see Yugara someday at least.

254
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:57,200
Kin'emon was talking
to me, not you, Karoo.

255
00:15:57,780 --> 00:15:59,604
Try waiting your turn for once.

256
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,410
Huh?

257
00:16:01,493 --> 00:16:04,097
Kin'emon was clearly getting
bored talking to you, Karoo.

258
00:16:04,180 --> 00:16:06,420
And since he is our esteemed guest,

259
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:09,537
I thought it would be
considerate of me to take over.

260
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:12,337
They're not going to start
fighting again, are they?

261
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:13,660
That's what they do.

262
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:15,978
Why don't you, Karoo, take a catnap?

263
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:17,851
I'll sleep when I'm dead.

264
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,837
I can help with that. Yeah?

265
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:21,517
You want to go another round?

266
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,659
That's fine with me, you three-man.

267
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:29,380
That's enough! Stop! Both
of you! Stop fighting!

268
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:35,497
What has transpired to
make you hate each other?

269
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:38,997
So, in days past, you two used
to be the best of friends.

270
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:42,357
I, uh, I forbid you to ever fight again,

271
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:45,477
and if it's over my father,
then it makes it even worse!

272
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:49,157
You know how much it would break his
heart to say this—it's too cruel!

273
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:50,070
Lord

274
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:54,217
Odin would?

275
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,130
would

276
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,150
Momo?

277
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:08,320
He said it would break his father's heart
to see this, but Kitaman's right here,

278
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:09,350
isn't he?

279
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,200
Please forgive us.

280
00:17:11,820 --> 00:17:14,232
Lord Momonosuke, you're absolutely right.

281
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,720
I'm ashamed of myself.

282
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:19,800
They both stopped!

283
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,320
I can't believe it.

284
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:23,049
Master is bowing his head.

285
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,520
That's who he is, I see.

286
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:36,700
I concur with what Lord Momonosuke says.

287
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:41,000
I must apologize for this deception.

288
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:47,800
As you may have surmised,
Lord Momonosuke is not my son.

289
00:17:58,520 --> 00:18:04,920
In all honesty, the boy that you see
before you is the son of Lord Kozuki Oden.

290
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:08,420
great daimyo of Kuri in the land of Wano.

291
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:18,400
This means Dogstorm, Catviper,
Kanjido, and myself honor him as lord.

292
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:20,760
The Kozuki have an heir?

293
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,840
That's a huge secret!

294
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:24,300
So what?

295
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:25,880
Momo is a big shot?

296
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:28,400
There are kings among his retainers.

297
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:31,200
He might be a lord with substantial power

298
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:36,017
If our true identities were
revealed during our travels I feared

299
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:39,717
that it might attract the attention
of deadly enemies Therefore,

300
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:42,840
we pretended to be father
and son Forgive me,

301
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:45,377
it's not that I did not
trust you So much as I

302
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:48,519
struggled to find the right
time to reveal the truth

303
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:56,400
I really thought you were a family
They are quite alike, such naughty boys

304
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:05,677
forgive me for deceiving you in truth
i am a lord yes and a naughty one

305
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:11,397
i'm no such thing who cares not me i
didn't ask for your opinion now bow

306
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:15,837
down to me luffy it's me if you think
we're gonna worship you all of a

307
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:21,020
sudden you need to get yourself a
reality check here shrimp lord momonosuke

308
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:34,080
There we go again, yet we
owe our lives to Sir Luffy.

309
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:36,240
He is a pirate after all.

310
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:37,695
Of course he's brash.

311
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:40,340
And he keeps our lord occupied.

312
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:45,440
Luffy's a brute!

313
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:47,880
Oh, how he fixes me, Onami!

314
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:50,060
Poor thing. Oh.

315
00:19:51,020 --> 00:19:55,340
Little brat, remove your
hand, lest I smite you. Hey.

316
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:02,900
By the way, Momo, if your
father is the Lord of Wano,

317
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:06,320
his castle must be full of treasure. Hey!

318
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:09,120
You're a really bad person, aren't you?

319
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:12,720
He faced that hardship only months ago.

320
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:14,350
Yes.

321
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:18,037
Their cheer is doing wonders.

322
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:19,700
It might just save him.

323
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:35,857
Let's make a truce.

324
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:38,197
If we keep dwelling on the past.

325
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:40,515
We'll just make the young lord suffer.

326
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:46,097
For his sake then.

327
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:48,597
I'll extend my hand as an ally.

328
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,500
But never as your friend!

329
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,420
and so it shall be.

330
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:01,320
My word!

331
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:03,980
They both made up? Really?

332
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:09,590
Unreal!

333
00:21:09,960 --> 00:21:12,200
I can't believe it! It's a miracle!

334
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:15,997
The king of the day and the
king of the night shaking hands?

335
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:18,198
That's the power of the Kozuki clan!

336
00:21:46,260 --> 00:21:48,557
We can climb the whale from here.

337
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:53,080
If you've got to learn which vines to
take, it's possible to reach the top.

338
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,774
And this is where Ryzo's hiding, right?

339
00:22:01,740 --> 00:22:03,960
Nin-nin! Ninja!

340
00:22:04,500 --> 00:22:06,320
Nin-nin! Ninja!

341
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,800
Nin-nin! Ninja!

342
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:10,290
Nin-nin!

343
00:22:10,373 --> 00:22:11,300
Nin-nin! Ninja!

344
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:14,420
It's a real-life ninja! Nin-nin!

345
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:16,680
He stalks the shadows! Nin-nin!

346
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:24,240
I'm starting to feel ill again, Kiyama.

347
00:22:24,660 --> 00:22:25,957
Should I take you down?

348
00:22:26,040 --> 00:22:28,511
Don't force yourself if you're truly sick.

349
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:35,780
It's just, the higher we go, the
louder the voice in my head gets.

350
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:43,320
Then be proud, your
father had the same power.

351
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:45,290
Indeed.

352
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:49,780
And he wasn't the only great man
who heard the voice. You're right.

353
00:22:50,060 --> 00:22:52,480
In fact, I was thinking the same thing.

354
00:23:00,580 --> 00:23:01,410
Wow!

355
00:23:01,540 --> 00:23:03,480
A real-life secret passage!

356
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:05,670
Whoa!

357
00:23:05,753 --> 00:23:08,260
On the tail of a whale!
Who'd have thunk it?

358
00:23:08,420 --> 00:23:11,537
Even if someone did come up
here, the door is well hidden.

359
00:23:11,620 --> 00:23:13,280
Follow me.

360
00:23:17,620 --> 00:23:20,520
It's a long fall to
the bottom. Don't slip.

361
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:32,960
What was that noise?

362
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:34,980
Race, without a doubt.

363
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:37,620
He's so close! Ninja!

364
00:23:39,540 --> 00:23:40,370
Ninja!

365
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,030
Oh!

366
00:23:47,113 --> 00:23:48,213
Get out of here, ninja!

367
00:23:49,380 --> 00:23:50,520
There he is.

368
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:53,080
Behold, Race, the great ninja.

369
00:23:53,860 --> 00:23:54,820
Oh, boy!

370
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:01,300
You've come at last, Cap Viper.

371
00:24:02,200 --> 00:24:03,030
Curse you!

372
00:24:03,140 --> 00:24:06,717
Why didn't you hand me over to the
enemy and spare your countrymen?

373
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:09,257
Everyone who brought me
food was grievously injured.

374
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:12,280
My heart could scarcely take it.

375
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:14,620
I was told this land is safe now.

376
00:24:14,880 --> 00:24:15,820
Is that true?

377
00:24:16,180 --> 00:24:21,060
If it fell to ruin while I was
held here, I'll never forgive you!

378
00:24:22,760 --> 00:24:23,590
Kaya!

379
00:24:32,900 --> 00:24:35,820
That's not what ninjas are like at all!

380
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:37,580
Who goes there?

381
00:24:37,740 --> 00:24:38,737
Are you invaders?

382
00:24:38,820 --> 00:24:39,702
Tell the truth!

383
00:24:39,820 --> 00:24:40,980
Why are you here?

384
00:24:44,140 --> 00:24:45,260
It's Raizo!

385
00:24:47,040 --> 00:24:47,870
Ah!

386
00:24:47,953 --> 00:24:51,000
Kin'emon, Kansuro, Lord Momonosuke!

387
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:52,820
And you're all well!

388
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:54,140
Thankfully so.

389
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:55,840
Raizo!

390
00:24:56,260 --> 00:24:57,420
You see that?

391
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:00,030
Huh?

392
00:25:04,260 --> 00:25:06,260
It's the crest of the Kozuki clan.

393
00:25:10,380 --> 00:25:12,237
Like Kinemon's tattoo.

394
00:25:12,320 --> 00:25:17,460
The crest here has adorned this
secret passage for centuries.

395
00:25:19,840 --> 00:25:25,360
And that stone, the deep red, I've
never seen one in such an odd color.

396
00:25:29,220 --> 00:25:31,520
Yeah, that is a poneglyph.

397
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:36,460
We know all about your
history, Nico Robin.

398
00:25:38,840 --> 00:25:42,580
I was told the people of
Ohara can read those words

399
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:48,960
So can you tell me what
makes this poneglyph unique?

400
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:53,697
None of the ones I've
encountered thus far were read.

401
00:25:53,780 --> 00:25:56,133
But I don't understand the significance.

402
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:58,540
This one has a different purpose.

403
00:26:01,020 --> 00:26:02,785
Perhaps you'd like to read it?

404
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:04,757
Yes, if you don't mind.

405
00:26:04,840 --> 00:26:06,257
Be my guest!

406
00:26:06,340 --> 00:26:07,540
Is something wrong?

407
00:26:08,040 --> 00:26:11,569
You've all been glaring at me
ever since you walked in here.

408
00:26:11,660 --> 00:26:13,560
Are you really a ninja?

409
00:26:14,500 --> 00:26:15,330
What?

410
00:26:15,413 --> 00:26:16,717
Are you questioning me?

411
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:18,897
Please excuse our friend's insolence.

412
00:26:18,980 --> 00:26:19,820
Worry not.

413
00:26:19,960 --> 00:26:22,380
The Straw Hat Pirates are fine allies.

414
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:23,880
They saved our lives.

415
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:24,920
Is that so?

416
00:26:25,220 --> 00:26:27,177
If you're really a ninja, prove it.

417
00:26:27,260 --> 00:26:29,200
Come on, throw a jerk in for me.

418
00:26:29,540 --> 00:26:31,560
And meditate under a waterfall.

419
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:34,937
Say nin and do some ninja magic.

420
00:26:35,020 --> 00:26:38,280
Oh, show us your Earth techniques first.

421
00:26:38,380 --> 00:26:40,117
But you've got to do fire next.

422
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:41,200
And water, too!

423
00:26:41,940 --> 00:26:43,700
You're asking too much of me.

424
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:46,620
Why do you pirates like ninjas so much?

425
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:49,233
It ain't because we're pirates, brother.

426
00:26:49,360 --> 00:26:50,190
Huh?

427
00:26:51,140 --> 00:26:52,540
Oooooooope! Super!

428
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:58,500
From the day they're born, every
man thinks ninjas are cool.

429
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:09,260
Oh, you guys are making me blush.

430
00:27:12,540 --> 00:27:15,580
Hey, ever go out with a
kunoichi, a lady ninja?

431
00:27:16,360 --> 00:27:17,948
Show us your jump training.

432
00:27:18,160 --> 00:27:19,866
Leap over some bamboo shoots.

433
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:23,062
You can do the shadow
clone technique, can't you?

434
00:27:23,640 --> 00:27:27,357
Do the thing where you hide in the
ceiling and get stabbed by a spear.

435
00:27:27,440 --> 00:27:29,717
Summon a giant frog and ride on his back.

436
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:32,557
Hold a scroll in your mouth and
say nin nin while you make pose it.

437
00:27:32,640 --> 00:27:33,977
No, that's enough.

438
00:27:34,060 --> 00:27:37,580
Stop imposing your
ninja stereotypes on me!

439
00:27:39,560 --> 00:27:41,540
Ninjas don't say Ni-Nin.

440
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:44,920
All of these ideas of yours are fantasy.

441
00:27:49,060 --> 00:27:51,740
You bear, you got a
weird body and no moves.

442
00:27:51,840 --> 00:27:53,016
How are you a ninja?

443
00:27:54,020 --> 00:27:54,980
It's true.

444
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:59,399
This physique of mine doesn't make
me terribly popular with Kunoichi.

445
00:27:59,740 --> 00:28:01,260
Hey, rude! Dude!

446
00:28:03,520 --> 00:28:04,480
Listen up.

447
00:28:05,340 --> 00:28:09,260
A true ninja master has a
quiet but resolute heart.

448
00:28:09,700 --> 00:28:13,537
One who lives in the shadows does
not put his techniques on display.

449
00:28:13,620 --> 00:28:15,760
Ninjutsu is not a mere party trick.

450
00:28:35,040 --> 00:28:35,870
Meatball!

451
00:28:36,900 --> 00:28:37,730
Huh?

452
00:28:37,813 --> 00:28:40,300
Smoke escaped to Higgs! Nyah!

453
00:28:44,460 --> 00:28:46,060
He disappeared!

454
00:28:47,260 --> 00:28:48,090
Huh?

455
00:28:48,420 --> 00:28:50,240
I didn't disappear at all!

456
00:28:53,820 --> 00:28:55,440
Why I'm right here?

457
00:28:55,620 --> 00:28:56,880
Whoa, that's wild!

458
00:29:00,840 --> 00:29:03,440
And here, too. And here.

459
00:29:03,840 --> 00:29:04,940
Oh, it's me.

460
00:29:06,460 --> 00:29:13,020
This is my shadow phone technique.

461
00:29:13,700 --> 00:29:14,640
That's awesome.

462
00:29:17,280 --> 00:29:20,060
You dare question my prowess?

463
00:29:20,620 --> 00:29:22,020
Flower shuriken.

464
00:29:23,840 --> 00:29:24,670
Shinobu.

465
00:29:24,753 --> 00:29:25,583
Shinobu!

466
00:29:34,220 --> 00:29:37,540
Invisible to the ladies,
invincible in battle!

467
00:29:39,340 --> 00:29:42,540
Rise all of the mist has arrived!

468
00:29:44,060 --> 00:29:44,890
Ha!

469
00:29:45,220 --> 00:29:46,640
All for free!

470
00:29:48,180 --> 00:29:50,100
With the story we got here!
